Relevant tables / columns and how they will be used  

• web_orders  
  – id : individual order (to be counted).  
  – account_id : joins to web_accounts so we know which company placed the order.  
  – total_amt_usd : dollar value of each order (to be summed).  

• web_accounts  
  – id : primary key; joins to web_orders.account_id.  
  – sales_rep_id : links each account to the representative who services it.  

• web_sales_reps  
  – id : joins to web_accounts.sales_rep_id.  
  – name : representative’s name for the report.  
  – region_id : links each rep to a geographic region.  

• web_region  
  – id : joins to web_sales_reps.region_id.  
  – name : readable region name; final report is grouped by this.  

Main conditions / join keys  
web_orders.account_id    = web_accounts.id  
web_accounts.sales_rep_id = web_sales_reps.id  
web_sales_reps.region_id  = web_region.id  

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  
Exploratory‑to‑final SQL (10 queries, each different and limited to 20 rows)

```sql
-- 1) List available regions
SELECT DISTINCT "id", "name"
FROM "web_region"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Peek at sales representatives and the region they belong to
SELECT DISTINCT "id", "name", "region_id"
FROM "web_sales_reps"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) How accounts map to reps (company, rep, region_id)
SELECT a."id"          AS account_id,
       a."name"        AS account_name,
       r."name"        AS rep_name,
       r."region_id"
FROM   "web_accounts"  AS a
JOIN   "web_sales_reps" AS r
       ON a."sales_rep_id" = r."id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Sample orders with their dollar value
SELECT "id"              AS order_id,
       "account_id",
       "total_amt_usd"
FROM   "web_orders"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Attach region name to each order (one line per order)
SELECT o."id"                 AS order_id,
       o."total_amt_usd",
       reg."name"             AS region
FROM   "web_orders"      AS o
JOIN   "web_accounts"    AS a   ON o."account_id"   = a."id"
JOIN   "web_sales_reps"  AS s   ON a."sales_rep_id" = s."id"
JOIN   "web_region"      AS reg ON s."region_id"    = reg."id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Number of orders per region
SELECT reg."name"                      AS region,
       COUNT(*)                        AS num_orders
FROM   "web_orders"       AS o
JOIN   "web_accounts"     AS a   ON o."account_id"   = a."id"
JOIN   "web_sales_reps"   AS s   ON a."sales_rep_id" = s."id"
JOIN   "web_region"       AS reg ON s."region_id"    = reg."id"
GROUP  BY reg."name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Total sales ($) per region
SELECT reg."name"                      AS region,
       ROUND(SUM(o."total_amt_usd"),2) AS total_sales
FROM   "web_orders"       AS o
JOIN   "web_accounts"     AS a   ON o."account_id"   = a."id"
JOIN   "web_sales_reps"   AS s   ON a."sales_rep_id" = s."id"
JOIN   "web_region"       AS reg ON s."region_id"    = reg."id"
GROUP  BY reg."name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Total sales by each rep (needed to find the top performer per region)
SELECT s."id"                       AS sales_rep_id,
       s."name"                     AS rep_name,
       reg."name"                   AS region,
       ROUND(SUM(o."total_amt_usd"),2) AS rep_total_sales
FROM   "web_orders"       AS o
JOIN   "web_accounts"     AS a   ON o."account_id"   = a."id"
JOIN   "web_sales_reps"   AS s   ON a."sales_rep_id" = s."id"
JOIN   "web_region"       AS reg ON s."region_id"    = reg."id"
GROUP  BY s."id", s."name", reg."name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Maximum rep sales per region (value only)
WITH rep_sales AS (
    SELECT s."id"   AS sales_rep_id,
           reg."id" AS region_id,
           ROUND(SUM(o."total_amt_usd"),2) AS rep_total_sales
    FROM   "web_orders" o
    JOIN   "web_accounts"   a ON o."account_id"   = a."id"
    JOIN   "web_sales_reps" s ON a."sales_rep_id" = s."id"
    JOIN   "web_region"     reg ON s."region_id"  = reg."id"
    GROUP  BY s."id", reg."id"
)
SELECT region_id,
       MAX(rep_total_sales) AS max_rep_sales
FROM   rep_sales
GROUP  BY region_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL REPORT ─ orders, region sales, and highest‑selling rep(s) (ties included)
WITH
rep_sales AS (        -- totals for every rep
    SELECT s."id"                AS sales_rep_id,
           s."name"              AS rep_name,
           reg."id"              AS region_id,
           reg."name"            AS region_name,
           SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS rep_total_sales
    FROM   "web_orders" o
    JOIN   "web_accounts"   a ON o."account_id"   = a."id"
    JOIN   "web_sales_reps" s ON a."sales_rep_id" = s."id"
    JOIN   "web_region"     reg ON s."region_id"  = reg."id"
    GROUP  BY s."id", reg."id"
),
region_agg AS (       -- overall regional figures
    SELECT reg."id"              AS region_id,
           reg."name"            AS region_name,
           COUNT(o."id")         AS num_orders,
           SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS region_total_sales
    FROM   "web_orders" o
    JOIN   "web_accounts"   a ON o."account_id"   = a."id"
    JOIN   "web_sales_reps" s ON a."sales_rep_id" = s."id"
    JOIN   "web_region"     reg ON s."region_id"  = reg."id"
    GROUP  BY reg."id"
),
max_rep_per_region AS (  -- maximum dollar amount in each region
    SELECT region_id,
           MAX(rep_total_sales) AS max_rep_sales
    FROM   rep_sales
    GROUP  BY region_id
),
top_reps AS (          -- all reps who hit that maximum (handles ties)
    SELECT r.region_id,
           GROUP_CONCAT(r.rep_name, ', ') AS top_rep_names,
           r.rep_total_sales             AS top_rep_sales
    FROM   rep_sales r
    JOIN   max_rep_per_region m
          ON r.region_id = m.region_id
         AND r.rep_total_sales = m.max_rep_sales
    GROUP  BY r.region_id
)
SELECT ra.region_name               AS region,
       ra.num_orders,
       ROUND(ra.region_total_sales,2)  AS total_sales_usd,
       tr.top_rep_names             AS highest_selling_rep_names,
       ROUND(tr.top_rep_sales,2)    AS rep_sales_usd
FROM   region_agg ra
LEFT  JOIN top_reps tr
       ON ra.region_id = tr.region_id
ORDER BY ra.region_name
LIMIT 20;
```

The last query delivers, for every region:
• total number of web orders  
• total dollar sales amount  
• the name(s) of the rep(s) who generated the highest sales in that region (comma‑separated if tied)  
• that top sales amount.
